6. Minimum Add to Make Parentheses Valid - Insertions needed

DYNAMIC PROGRAMMING FORMULATION
==============================

Another approach using DP:
dp[i][j] = combinations using i open and j close parentheses (j ≤ i)

dp[0][0] = [""]
dp[i][j] = ["(" + combo for combo in dp[i-1][j]] + 
           [")" + combo for combo in dp[i][j-1]]
           (with bound checks)

ADVANCED OPTIMIZATION: O(1) SPACE FOR VALIDATION
===============================================

Space Complexity Improvement:
- Use integer counters instead of recursion stack
- Iterative approach for large n

public static List<String> generateParenthesesIterative(int n) {
    List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();
    List<String> current = new ArrayList<>();
    List<Integer> openCounts = new ArrayList<>();
    List<Integer> closeCounts = new ArrayList<>();

    current.add("");
    openCounts.add(0);
    closeCounts.add(0);

    while (!current.isEmpty()) {
        String cur = current.remove(current.size() - 1);
        int openCnt = openCounts.remove(openCounts.size() - 1);
        int closeCnt = closeCounts.remove(closeCounts.size() - 1);

        if (cur.length() == 2 * n) {
            result.add(cur);
            continue;
        }

        if (openCnt < n) {
            current.add(cur + "(");
            openCounts.add(openCnt + 1);
            closeCounts.add(closeCnt);
        }
        if (closeCnt < openCnt) {
            current.add(cur + ")");
            openCounts.add(openCnt);
            closeCounts.add(closeCnt + 1);
        }
    }
    return result;
}

SAMPLE USAGE
===========

